Z||000004||fierosound||12-31-1999||04:51 PM||||I agree, it is very pricey.  I wouldn't spend that kind of cash.  But people had been asking, and I thought I'd pass along what I had found.<P>Something that works almost as well and is more econpmical is to install "low energy tires" on your car.  I bought some Michelin tires of this type.  Because of the low rolling resistance in the construction of the tire, the effort required to steer the car is also reduce very noticeably.  No more "grunt" required when parking, and one handed driving becomes the norm even running 205R60-15 on front, 215R60-15 on rear.||||reg||10
